## Database Schema Versioning & Migration Standards

Mobile application updates must never crash or wipe local user data due to unhandled SQLite/database schema mutations:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    V1["Database Schema V1\n(Shipped in App v1.0)"] -->|"Migration 1 -> 2\n(Add nullable column)"| V2
    V2["Database Schema V2\n(Shipped in App v1.2)"] -->|"Migration 2 -> 3\n(Create new table & index)"| V3
    V3["Database Schema V3\n(Shipped in App v2.0)"]

    classDef default fill:#13251c,stroke:#1f3b2c,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#e2e8f0;
    classDef step fill:#1b3826,stroke:#22c55e,stroke-width:2px,color:#f3d17b;
    class V1,V2,V3 step;
```

### Mandatory Migration Rules:
1. **Never Use Destructive Fallbacks in Production:** Android's `.fallbackToDestructiveMigration()` and iOS CoreData `NSMigratePersistentStoresAutomaticallyOption` without model versioning are strictly prohibited in release builds.
2. **Nullable Columns for Schema Expansion:** All new columns added to existing tables must either be `NULLABLE` or specify a safe default value (`DEFAULT 0`, `DEFAULT ''`).
3. **Mandatory Automated Migration Tests:** Every schema modification PR must include an automated unit test verifying that database files from version $N-1$ upgrade successfully to version $N$ with existing sample records intact.

