## Architectural Non-Negotiables & Prohibitions

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">DATA PERSISTENCE BOUNDARY RULES</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>1. No Main Thread Database I/O:</strong> Never execute SQLite queries, CoreData fetches, or disk writes on the UI main thread. All database interactions must execute on background threads (<code>Dispatchers.IO</code> in Kotlin, background Swift actors, or asynchronous threads).</li>
    <li><strong>2. Plain-Text Secrets Prohibited:</strong> Sensitive customer tokens, passwords, and private API keys must never be stored in plain SQLite columns or standard UserDefaults/SharedPreferences. Secrets belong exclusively in Android KeyStore or iOS Keychain.</li>
    <li><strong>3. Idempotency Keys Required on Mutations:</strong> Every mutating outbox record must include a unique client-generated UUID sent via the <code>X-Idempotency-Key</code> header to prevent duplicate charges or orders during flaky cellular reconnects.</li>
    <li><strong>4. Mandatory Eviction Policy for Caches:</strong> Unconstrained local caching leads to app bloating and OS storage purges. All cached entity tables must implement time-to-live (TTL) pruning or LRU (Least Recently Used) eviction rules.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

